      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-26463",
      ":question/problem": "Calls to city A cost $$7$ per minute, while calls to city B cost $$5$ per minute. Let $x$ be the time (in minutes) a company employee spends calling city A, and let $y$ be the time (in minutes) they spend calling city B.\n\nWhich of the following shaded regions represents all possible combinations $(x, y)$ of calls to both cities the employee can make if their maximum budget for all calls is $$35$?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
