      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-29526",
      ":question/problem": "At a certain electronics store, each microcontroller is sold for a profit of $$300$ and each integrated circuit for a profit of $$200$. Let $x$ be the number of microcontrollers sold and let $y$ be the number of integrated circuits sold.\n\nWhich of the following shaded regions represents all possible combinations $(x, y)$ of components sold if they expect to make a profit greater than $$1200$?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
    }
